note Source: node/lib/events.js, EventEmitter.init (lines 332-354). JavaScript, I/O (adversarial).

note GAP: map from event name to listeners with a null prototype - `{ __proto__: null }` is a dictionary keyed by strings or symbols. The doc has List but no Map/Dictionary type. Invented: `a Map from EventKey to Listeners` and `an empty Map`.
note GAP: symbol-keyed properties - `this[kShapeMode]` and `this[kCapture]` are hidden properties keyed by module-private Symbols. Modelled as ordinary fields.
note GAP: missing fields that may be absent or undefined - `_events`, `_maxListeners` and the options object may be undefined. Modelled with `maybe`.
type EventEmitter
    field events as a maybe Map from EventKey to Listeners
    field events_count as a Nat
    field shape_mode as a Bool
    field max_listeners as a maybe Number
    field capture as a Bool

type EventEmitterOptions
    note GAP: dynamic value type - `opts.captureRejections` can be any JS value; validateBoolean checks at run time that it is a boolean. Modelled as `maybe Unknown`.
    field capture_rejections as a maybe Unknown

note validateBoolean throws ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE if value is not a boolean.
to validate_boolean value named name
    given value is an Unknown
    given name is Text
    produces a Bool
    fails with InvalidArgType

note GAP: prototype chain - `ObjectGetPrototypeOf(this)._events` reads the `_events` of the object this one inherits from, and `EventEmitter.prototype[kCapture]` reads module-level mutable state (EventEmitter.captureRejections writes it). Scribe has no inheritance, prototypes or module state. Invented: `prototype_of` as an operation and `default_capture` as a field of a capability passed in.
to prototype_of emitter
    given emitter is an EventEmitter
    produces a maybe EventEmitter

type EmitterDefaults
    field default_capture as a Bool

note WORKAROUND: `this` - init is called with `this` bound to a new or subclass instance (EventEmitter.call(this, opts)). It becomes an editable parameter.
note WORKAROUND: optional argument - `opts` may be omitted. It becomes `a maybe EventEmitterOptions`.
note UNCLEAR: allocation - `{ __proto__: null }` allocates; the doc says any allocating operation must take an Allocator. Added `memory`.
to init emitter with opts using defaults and memory
    given emitter is an editable EventEmitter
    given opts is a maybe EventEmitterOptions
    given defaults is an EmitterDefaults
    given memory is an Allocator
    fails with InvalidArgType, OutOfMemory
    uses defaults, memory

    note GAP: identity comparison - `this._events === proto._events` asks whether two references point at the same object (shared with the prototype). Scribe has no reference identity; `is` compares values. Invented: `is the same object as`.
    var events_shared starts at false
    choose prototype_of emitter
        when some proto
            if events of emitter is the same object as events of proto
                set events_shared to true
        when nothing
            set events_shared to false
    if events of emitter is nothing or events_shared
        set events of emitter to some (an empty Map using memory)
        set events_count of emitter to 0
        set shape_mode of emitter to false
    otherwise
        set shape_mode of emitter to true

    note WORKAROUND: `||=` on a falsy value - `this._maxListeners ||= undefined` turns any falsy value (0, NaN, null, undefined) into undefined and leaves the property as an own property. With a typed maybe Number only 0 can be falsy; NaN has no spelling and own-property creation has no meaning.
    choose max_listeners of emitter
        when some limit
            if limit is 0
                set max_listeners of emitter to nothing
        when nothing
            set max_listeners of emitter to nothing

    note WORKAROUND: optional chaining with truthiness - `opts?.captureRejections` is truthy for any non-false, non-zero, non-empty value. The truthiness test is approximated by `is_truthy`, which the doc does not have.
    note WORKAROUND: no-op branch - `choose` must handle every case, and the doc shows no way to write an empty `when` arm, so the `nothing` arms below repeat an assignment that changes nothing.
    note UNCLEAR: `var raw_capture starts at nothing` - the doc does not say how the type of a variable is fixed when its first value is `nothing`, and has no type annotation on `var`.
    var capture_given starts at false
    var raw_capture starts at nothing
    choose opts
        when some options
            choose capture_rejections of options
                when some value
                    if is_truthy value
                        set capture_given to true
                        set raw_capture to some value
                when nothing
                    set capture_given to false
        when nothing
            set capture_given to false

    if capture_given
        choose raw_capture
            when some value
                note `Boolean(opts.captureRejections)` is the value itself once validated
                set capture of emitter to try validate_boolean value named "options.captureRejections"
            when nothing
                set capture of emitter to default_capture of defaults
    otherwise
        note Assigning the capture field directly saves an expensive prototype lookup in a very sensitive hot path.
        set capture of emitter to default_capture of defaults

note helper for JavaScript truthiness; Scribe has no implicit conversion, so this has to be an explicit operation
to is_truthy value
    given value is an Unknown
    produces a Bool
